      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The US intervention in Iraq was a clear example of a nation prioritizing its own geopolitical interests over the stated moral mandate to stop genocide, as the primary justification was regime change rather than immediate humanitarian relief.\nWhen a country uses \"human rights\" as a convenient cover for power grabs, it is indeed a hollow label that betrays the very essence of democracy by placing national ambition above human dignity.\nWe can distinguish these cases by examining whether the stated moral goals were the primary driver of the action or merely a post-hoc excuse for self-serving agendas.\nA true democracy must be willing to sacrifice its own interests to uphold universal rights, and when it chooses the former, it has fundamentally failed its moral foundation.",
